#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128893 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"}] :question/id #uuid "09499f38-a497-5f59-9cb2-0882a5853320" :question/math-academy-id "e-3368" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z) = x^2+y^2+z^2,$ find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,-2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z) = k$ at the point $(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\nabla \\! f(x_0,y_0,z_0) \\cdot \\langle x-x_0, \\: y-y_0, \\: z-z_0 \\rangle  = 0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(x_0,y_0,z_0) =(2,-2,1)\\mathbin{:}$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}\\,i+{f}_{y}\\,j+{f}_{z}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2x\\text{ }i+2y\\text{ }j+2z\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,-2,1) & =2(2)\\text{ }i+2(-2)\\text{ }j+2(1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i-4\\,j+2\\text{ }k \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-4\\,,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,-2,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-(-2),\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,\\,-4,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-2)-4(y+2)+2(z-1) & =0 \\\\ 4x-4y+2z-18 & =0 \\\\ 2x-2y+z-9 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128998 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "9091e2dc-5b05-5ae7-a498-9de0483ec375" :question/math-academy-id "e-6183" :question/problem "Consider the surface $z^3y^2 =x^2-5.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to this surface at the point $(-1,2,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{3}{y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}-5 \\\\ {z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z) = z^3y^2 - x^2,$ our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=-5.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z) = k$ at the point $(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x_0,y_0,z_0) \\cdot \\langle x-x_0, \\: y-y_0, \\: z-z_0 \\rangle  = 0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(-1,2,-1)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(-2x)\\text{ }i+2{z}^{3}y\\text{ }j+3{z}^{2}{y}^{2}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(-1,2,-1) & =(-2)(-1)\\text{ }i+2(-1)^{3}(2)\\text{ }j+3(-1)^{2}(2)^{2}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2\\,i-4j+12\\,k \\\\  & =⟨2,-4,12⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,2,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-(-1),\\,y-2,\\,z-(-1)⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2,-4,12⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-2,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2(x+1)-4(y-2)+12(z+1) & =0 \\\\ 2x-4y+12z+22 & =0 \\\\ x-2y+6z+11 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e1cb627-a7ce-5590-948c-7c7032f79d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+3y-z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475533} {:answer/id #uuid "3f9862fd-f15b-56b9-9ff9-a1f3fd633b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+y-2z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475535} {:answer/id #uuid "44dad19a-e64e-50a5-86cd-7127f23c8c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+y-z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475546} {:answer/id #uuid "4678691a-7e4b-5fd9-8289-5d20781d9432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x+3y-z-7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475548} {:answer/id #uuid "845682f9-4cee-5b66-a8be-87fafd6313ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+y+z-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e1cb627-a7ce-5590-948c-7c7032f79d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+3y-z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475533} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd5c8610-318e-58b9-8590-725b9e0fa2c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "58a67d8c-4e10-594d-863e-d6da9c98fcce" :question/math-academy-id "q-102707" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z+{z}^{2}y+{y}^{2}x$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes  through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,1,-1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}z+{z}^{2}y+{y}^{2}x)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}z+{z}^{2}y+{y}^{2}x)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}z+{z}^{2}y+{y}^{2}x)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(2xz+{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+({z}^{2}+2yx)\\text{ }j+({x}^{2}+2zy)k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1,-1) & =(2(1)(-1)+{1}^{2})\\text{ }i+((-1)^{2}+2(1)(1))\\text{ }j+({1}^{2}+2(-1)(1))k \\\\  & =-\\,i+3\\,j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,3,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-1,3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ -(x-1)+3(y-1)-(z+1) & =0 \\\\ -x+3y-z-3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554541 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "065677e5-6668-589c-8f82-28615b7c7eea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-6y+z-13=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553881} {:answer/id #uuid "8da732bc-eb58-5338-abe0-8d52e81e25e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+8y-5z+12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554168} {:answer/id #uuid "bd87e438-6635-5fc8-8041-e85ff749d4dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+9y-z+16=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554281} {:answer/id #uuid "d50bfffc-a66c-5b56-a37e-a72964286f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+5y-6z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554332} {:answer/id #uuid "ea005b66-1e1f-575c-a788-5fbfb346d025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+8y-6z+30=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea005b66-1e1f-575c-a788-5fbfb346d025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x+8y-6z+30=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554379} :answer-field/id #uuid "74e95cce-259a-58bc-a6dc-cf74c51c993b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "138bcf11-9efc-57ee-ad7b-ef21818db0e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-102712" :question/problem "Consider the surface ${z}^{2}y+16=4\\sqrt{x}+y.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(4,-1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}y+16 & =4\\sqrt{x}+y. \\\\ {z}^{2}y-4\\sqrt{x}-y & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)={z}^{2}y-4\\sqrt{x}-y$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=-16.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(4,-1,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{2}y-4\\sqrt{x}-y)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{2}y-4\\sqrt{x}-y)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2}y-4\\sqrt{x}-y)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}\\text{ }i+({z}^{2}-1)\\text{ }j+2zy\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(4,-1,3) & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4}}\\text{ }i+({3}^{2}-1)\\text{ }j+2(3)(-1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =-\\,i+8\\text{ }j-6\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-1,8,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(4,-1,3)\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y+1,\\,z-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-1,8,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y+1,\\,z-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ -(x-4)+8(y+1)-6(z-3) & =0 \\\\ -x+8y-6z+30 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475934 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06ddc08d-d22f-5193-bf06-38fb8c7ba7c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475455} {:answer/id #uuid "0af3f2c2-59c9-5249-a2d8-811877a6ca18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475461} {:answer/id #uuid "19987fb0-bc40-51ba-b84d-d8cb0087f00a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475476} {:answer/id #uuid "226d0641-c568-50b8-93be-58d7db8760ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475487} {:answer/id #uuid "87b7e1f6-b074-5206-8b9b-5827ab7b73bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0af3f2c2-59c9-5249-a2d8-811877a6ca18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475461} :answer-field/id #uuid "32ad6879-6146-512a-b9ce-7b997929ffe5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "480ef21f-535f-5e73-9903-6cc50742dda8" :question/math-academy-id "q-102713" :question/problem "Consider the surface $z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)-xyz=2+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}.$ Given that $n=⟨a,b,c⟩$ is a non-zero normal vector to the surface at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2},2),$ what is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define  $f(x,y,z)=z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)-xyz.$ Then, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=2+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{2}.$  \n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2},2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)-xyz)i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)-xyz)j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)-xyz)k \\\\  & =(-z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)-yz)i+(-z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)-xz)j+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)-xy)k \\\\ ∇f(\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2},2) & =(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-2(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\\text{ }i+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-2(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\\text{ }j+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{\\pi }{2})(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\pi \\text{ }i-\\pi \\text{ }j+(1+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =⟨\\pi ,\\,-\\pi ,\\,1+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩=⟨\\pi ,\\,-\\pi ,\\,\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}+4}{4}⟩.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{\\pi }{-\\pi }=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64714f8f-6e99-5b47-ad35-de287d9165d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2y-4z+15=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475591} {:answer/id #uuid "7117415a-5ef5-5b3e-832a-e0fb18a5246f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-3y+2z-11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475601} {:answer/id #uuid "8b61f94e-dc56-526e-824a-66c203febdf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+4y+z-10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475653} {:answer/id #uuid "9c45389e-541e-5ac3-aa83-a1435e6c3bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+4y-4z+18=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475673} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a78e06-677c-5f95-89c0-1f507b59be9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y-3z+11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c45389e-541e-5ac3-aa83-a1435e6c3bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+4y-4z+18=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475673} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5f7cc0c-f2cb-5ebd-8a19-e3ddc8cdda4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2dcb9c2a-7362-5965-b423-4b434eec8d3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-102714" :question/problem "Consider the surface $x{y}^{2}+6=z{x}^{2}.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(-2,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{2}+6 & =z{x}^{2} \\\\ x{y}^{2}-z{x}^{2} & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}-z{x}^{2}$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=-6.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(-2,-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2}-z{x}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{2}-z{x}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{y}^{2}-z{x}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =({y}^{2}-2xz)\\text{ }i+2xy\\text{ }j-{x}^{2}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(-2,-1,1) & =((-1)^{2}-2(-2)(1))\\text{ }i+2(-2)(-1)\\text{ }j-(-2)^{2}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =5\\,i+4j-4\\,k \\\\  & =⟨5,4,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-2,-1,1)\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨5,4,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 5(x+2)+4(y+1)-4(z-1) & =0 \\\\ 5x+4y-4z+18 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129596 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13a034a0-40db-53e2-8743-0500f64927fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,-e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-e,\\,y-e,\\,z-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493426} {:answer/id #uuid "4d8e49ba-c572-585b-9000-22f731c9e31c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e,e,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493516} {:answer/id #uuid "7fd70068-b6fc-58b5-a8fd-0b6d0f6cdc1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,-e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493590} {:answer/id #uuid "a4259989-16f4-5162-93ea-522cff1adbaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493652} {:answer/id #uuid "b48376c2-fa7d-5ea7-a3f5-9c2f64a3454e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e,e,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+1,\\,z+e⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d8e49ba-c572-585b-9000-22f731c9e31c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e,e,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493516} :answer-field/id #uuid "675858d2-09f1-5094-a85f-2db7923cff6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39528896-10e8-5126-bdec-f26e9bdcc487" :question/math-academy-id "q-36334" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{y}-z$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,e).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,1,e):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{y}-z)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y}-z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{e}^{y}-z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & ={e}^{y}\\text{ }i+x{e}^{y}\\text{ }j-k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1,e) & ={e}^{1}\\text{ }i+(1){e}^{1}\\text{ }j-k \\\\  & =e\\,i+e\\,j-k \\\\  & =⟨e,e,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1,e)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨e,e,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129598 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81080468-c2ff-5b57-894c-06513974031d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - y - z + 17 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127070} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1aff9c-ae98-52d1-aaf5-a9e694ed1419" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x - y - z + 27 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127071} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ccc0f7-b586-5a3c-8853-180ca809aa0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x - 8y - z + 17 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127072} {:answer/id #uuid "05707541-b792-5871-a703-edcab81ff57f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - 8y - z + 7 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127073} {:answer/id #uuid "7b82f780-8215-538d-ba71-58e7316b3c1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x - 8y - 3z + 4 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127074}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0242716f-bffc-52a5-9308-d0d4f01e04ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127069}] :question/id #uuid "762d594d-7e6d-57b6-aecd-e43c658c860d" :question/math-academy-id "q-36390" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x, y, z) = 8x - y^{2} - z$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x, y, z) = (2, 4, 1)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129600 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d58667f-c4b7-52cb-8104-74416f25b43d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x - y + 4z + 1 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127082} {:answer/id #uuid "1e4fe789-dd4d-56e2-a9c5-8838acc23083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - y + z + 4 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127083} {:answer/id #uuid "21a7a8ba-b796-59ca-bbc3-902627ce297d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x - y + 4z - 8 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127084} {:answer/id #uuid "704ca0b4-4316-5515-8ef2-478821a77123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - y + z + 1 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127085} {:answer/id #uuid "788dd523-c670-5248-91e2-381188b0b911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x - 4z + 12 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127086}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d23e2841-0f8c-5a43-85eb-97c15c263fb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127081}] :question/id #uuid "fd4de585-73eb-5c7c-8651-4f10cf9e9440" :question/math-academy-id "q-36764" :question/problem "Consider the surface $z^{2}x^{2} = xy$. Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(1, 4, 2)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348450 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "055ca543-5d57-5d9e-a2d2-381ab5780193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345399} {:answer/id #uuid "606d26e9-38fb-5406-81c6-bbbc70b87d52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346185} {:answer/id #uuid "8e4a5312-9c03-5d11-93e6-1b83c3444d97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346589} {:answer/id #uuid "c345d148-9371-50cb-bc70-e50fb33e6977" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347038} {:answer/id #uuid "dcdb03f8-d803-5843-ae32-5f7feed10058" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c345d148-9371-50cb-bc70-e50fb33e6977" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347038} :answer-field/id #uuid "38edd513-af3d-5da1-9d87-d229b9ce95f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "581af8f1-8855-519d-a20e-429c65cef0c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-80778" :question/problem "Consider the surface ${2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}=2.$ Given that $n=⟨a,b,c⟩$ is a non-zero normal vector to the surface at the point $(1,-1,1),$ what is the value of $\\frac{c}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define  $f(x,y,z)={2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}.$ Then, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=2.$  \n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(1,-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy})i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy})j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy})k \\\\  & =({2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}\\cdot 2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)i+({2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}\\cdot 2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)j+({2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}\\cdot 6z\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)k \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2(y\\,\\text{ }{2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}\\text{ }i+x\\,\\text{ }{2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}\\text{ }j+3z\\,\\text{ }{2}^{3{z}^{2}+2xy}\\text{ }k) \\\\ ∇f(1,-1,1) & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2((-1)\\cdot \\text{ }{2}^{3(1)^{2}+2\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)}\\text{ }i+1\\cdot \\,\\text{ }{2}^{3(1)^{2}+2\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)}\\text{ }j+3(1)\\cdot {2}^{3(1)^{2}+2\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)}\\text{ }k) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2(-{2}^{1}\\text{ }i+{2}^{1}\\text{ }j+3\\cdot {2}^{1}\\text{ }k) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2(-i+j+3\\text{ }k) \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,12\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩=⟨-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,12\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{c}{b}=\\frac{12\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}=3.$"}]}
